[Start "two-knights-na5 5.exd5"]

5... Na5 { Chases the bishop away. Never play 5...Nxd5? 6.Nxf7, the Fried Liver Attack, which wins for White. } ( 5... Nxd5 $2 6. Nxf7 Kxf7 7. Qf3+ Ke6 8. Nc3 ) 6. Bb5+ c6 { Hits the bishop and the pawn on d5 together. } 7. dxc6 bxc6 8. Be2 h6 { Asks the knight on g5 to leave before it can go to f7. } 9. Nf3 e4 { Hits the knight again and opens the bishop on c8. } 10. Ne5 Bd6 { Attacks the knight again and prepares to castle. Black is a pawn down but has the better development. } *
